DATASET_TITLE Crosswind and Tripped Rollover
#RingCtrl8 1
#RingCtrl9 1

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example demonstrates an Event-driven test where an SUV with a roof load is driving along a coastal highway, slowly drifts off the road, and encounters a wind gust.
#
#As the SUV reaches the edge of the road, it encounters a gust of wind from the gap in the cliff to the left. The wind gust nudges the vehicle onto the shoulder which is lower than the road surface and has a lower coefficient of friction than the road. The driver overreacts, rapidly applying a steering wheel input to steer the vehicle back onto the road surface. The sudden steer input induces large yaw and roll moments, and the front right wheel experiences a very large lateral force, the results of which are a tripped rollover.
#
#This vehicle uses tire datasets which do not use the user-defined tire contact patch dimensions. Browse to the Vehicle: Assembly screen by clicking on the Vehicle: Loads, Sensors, etc. blue link "E-Class, SUV w/ Roof Load (Single Pt. Tire).
#
#Once on the Vehicle: Loads, Sensors, etc. screen, click on the vehicle blue link to browse to the Vehicle: Assembly screen and click on the tire dataset "265/75 R16 (Single Contact Point)" for more information.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: CarSim Run Control; { Extended Models } Crosswind and Tripped Rollover
